From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:45:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] KitKat UI P24: opaque shade panel/header, carrier label
 anti-pop

- 24.1 kitkat_shade_panel_bg (flat #ff161616, P3 palette): donor 4.4
  status_bar_expanded was an OPAQUE panel riding the PanelView
  expansion over the wallpaper, never a translucent scrim fade. New
  kitkat_shade_panel_bg view in the shade container reveals top-down
  with the expansion fraction (clip rect, no per-frame requestLayout)
  in NotificationsQSContainerController - GONE outside the unlocked
  SHADE state so the keyguard shade and its scrims are untouched.
- 24.2 combined_qs_header: opaque kitkat_shade_header_bg strip on the
  donor header band - the clock/date/settings/clear-all sat on the
  wallpaper before; the strip guarantees the contrast the retired
  translucent pills were faking (P18.5 zeroed the unlocked scrims, so
  nothing backed the header).
- 24.3 ic_notify_button_bg: default state transparent, pressed
  highlight only - donor semantics; the resting translucent overlay
  read as a tacky pill under the clock, gear and clear-all X. Pill
  background retired from the clock (was enabled=false, never
  pressable). Buttons keep the pressed feedback.
- 24.4 NotificationShadeDepthController: zero shade blur/zoom in the
  UNLOCKED SHADE state - donor 4.4 had no blur, and the opaque panel
  hides the blurred window background at full expansion anyway.
  Keyguard states keep the stock treatment.
- 24.5 CarrierTextManager: static last-info cache replayed the moment
  a listener attaches - the telephony recompute lands asynchronously
  (often mid-shade), which made the carrier label pop in after the
  shade was already open. Shared by the keyguard label, the shade
  header carrier group and the shade footer label; the async recompute
  still corrects SIM-state changes.
- 24.6 ShadeCarrierTextController: fade in the first non-empty carrier
  label (200ms) instead of popping; landed at full alpha when the fade
  is interrupted by closing the shade.

Change-Id: I1af4cee17217479c23466d7557fd09dac197efb9
